<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S6.T5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>. </span><span id="S6.T5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">System-level comparison across standard (Prompt = 1k, Gen = 128) and agentic (Prompt = 5.6k, Gen = 85k) workloads. For fairness, we use four A100 GPUs with a total HBM capacity of 320 GB as the reference. PLENA and MicroScopiQ are both assumed to have four cores and identical HBM configurations, including capacity and bandwidth. The selected configurations are listed in <a href="#A1.T17" title="In A.11. Compute Performance Experiment Settings ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Combating the Memory Walls: Optimization Pathways for Long-Context Agentic LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>. Since the GPU’s silicon area includes significant overhead for non-compute functionality, we ensure that the multiplier count is matched across systems for a balanced comparison.</span></figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
