<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3. </span>Selective Rotation</h3>

<figure id="A1.T10" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T10.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 10</span>. </span><span id="A1.T10.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">This table investigates the effect of online rotation on activations in the linear layers. For the LLaMA2-7B model, applying rotation to the <span id="A1.T10.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">down_proj</span> layer results in worse performance compared to not rotating it, whereas this effect is not observed in the LLaMA3-8B model. Moreover, rotating the <span id="A1.T10.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">o_proj</span> layer severely degrades the performance of LLaMA3-8B. These results suggest that the effectiveness of rotation is highly model-dependent.</span></figcaption>
